* {{audio|en|En-us-simple.ogg|Audio (GA)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|sim|ple}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪmpəl|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# [[uncomplicated|Uncomplicated]]; lacking complexity; taken by itself, with nothing added.
#* {{RQ:Hough Purchase Price|chapter=I|text=We are engaged in a great work, a treatise on our river fortifications, perhaps? But since when did army officers afford the luxury of amanuenses in this '''simple''' republic?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1940|author=Rosetta E. Clarkson|title=Green Enchantments: The Magic Spell of Gardens |publisher=The Macmillan Company|page=253|text=Primitive people, colossally ignorant of the cause of disease and of curative processes, attributed to supernatural agencies any causes and effects for which their '''simple''' minds could give no natural explanations.}}
# [[easy|Easy]]; not difficult.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=Sydney I. Landau|title=Dictionaries: The Art and Craft of Lexicography|publisher=Cambridge University Press|isbn=0-521-78512-X|page=167
|passage=There is no '''simple''' way to define precisely a complex arrangement of parts, however homely the object may appear to be.}}
# Without [[ornamentation]]; [[plain]].
# Free from [[duplicity]]; [[guileless]], [[innocent]], [[straightforward]].
#* {{RQ:Marston Dutch Courtezan|passage=Full many fine men go upon my score, as '''simple''' as I stand here, and I trust them.}}
#* {{RQ:Byron Childe Harold|canto=I|stanza=XXXVI|passage=Must thou trust Tradition's '''simple''' tongue?}}
#* {{RQ:Emerson Complete Works|volume=I|page=160|passage=Nothing is more '''simple''' than greatness; indeed, to be '''simple''' is to be great. The vision of genius comes by renouncing the too officious activity of the understanding, and giving leave and amplest privilege to the spontaneous sentiment.}}
# [[undistinguished|Undistinguished]] in social condition; of no special [[rank]].
#* {{quote-av
|en
|date=April 24, 1995
|title=w:Improbable Cause
|series={{w|Star Trek: Deep Space Nine}}
|publisher=w:Paramount Domestic Television
|genre=Science Fiction
|season=3
|issue=20
|oclc=1027641849
|passage={{w|Elim Garak|Garak}}: Who would want to kill me, a '''simple''' tailor? / {{w|Odo (Star Trek)|Odo}}: A '''simple''' tailor? A '''simple''' tailor who used to be an agent of the {{w|Obsidian Order}}!}}
#: {{antonyms|en|gentle}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} [[trivial|Trivial]]; [[insignificant]].
#* {{RQ:Malory Le Morte Darthur|book=X|chapter=LV|passage=‘That was a '''symple''' cause,’ seyde Sir Trystram, ‘for to sle a good knyght for seyynge well by his maystir.’|brackets=off|termlang=en|translation=‘That was a simple cause,’ said Sir Tristram, ‘for to slay a good knight for to say well by his master.’ }}
# {{lb|en|now|colloquial|euphemism}} Feeble-minded; [[foolish]].
# {{lb|en|heading|technical}} Structurally uncomplicated.
## {{lb|en|chemistry|pharmacology}} Consisting of one [[single]] substance; [[uncompounded]].
## {{lb|en|mathematics}} Of a group: having no [[normal]] [[subgroup]].
## {{lb|en|botany}} Not [[compound]], but possibly [[lobed]].
## Using [[steam]] only once in its [[cylinders]], in contrast to a [[compound]] engine, where steam is used more than once in [[high-pressure]] and [[low-pressure]] cylinders. {{q|of a steam engine}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1959|title=Steam's Finest Hour|editor=David P. Morgan|publisher=Kalmbach Publishing Co.|page=6
|passage=Chesapeake & Ohio turned to '''simple''' articulateds, for instance, simply because its Alleghany tunnels would not accommodate the low-pressure forward cylinders of larger compounds.}}
## {{lb|en|zoology}} Consisting of a single individual or [[zooid]]; not [[compound]].
##: {{ux|en|a '''simple''' ascidian}}
## {{lb|en|mineralogy}} [[homogenous|Homogenous]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Mere; not other than; being only.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare All's Well|act=II|scene=i|passage=A medicine {{...}} whose '''simple''' touch / Is powerful to araise King Pepin.}}

